course: dictionary
lesson: 873
title: Billionth: first in a billion, or one tiny part
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Billionth is a number word, like first, second or hundredth. It can tell you a position in a line: the billionth thing is number one billion, written 1,000,000,000th.
explain: Billionth can also name a part. One billionth is one of a billion equal parts, written 1/1,000,000,000. Words like billionths are the plural form, and they are also used as nouns.
explain: «A computer chip has billions of tiny switches... the newest chips are described in nanometres, billionths of a metre.» The word billions is a clue: it is a very big number. So billionths of a metre are tiny pieces of a metre, and a nanometre is one of them.
fact: Billionth means coming as number one billion in order: 1,000,000,000th.
fact: Billionth can also mean one of a billion equal parts: 1/1,000,000,000.
fact: A billion is 1,000,000,000, a thousand million.
fact: A nanometre is a billionth of a metre, so it is much smaller than a millimetre.
fact: A nanosecond is a billionth of a second.
exercise: «The newest chips are described in nanometres, billionths of a metre.» In this sentence, billionths means | Very large numbers of metres | *One of a billion equal parts | Tiny switches on a chip | The number of chips in a box
exercise: Which number is the billionth? | *1,000,000,000th | 1,000th | 1,000,000th | 100th
exercise: In «A computer chip has billions of tiny switches», what does billions mean? | One tiny part of a switch | A small group of chips | *Very large numbers, a thousand million or more | The first number in a list
test: A nanosecond is a billionth of a second. What does that mean? | A second with exactly one tick | A second that lasts a billion years | *A second cut into a billion equal parts, so it is tiny | A very long second
test: Which phrase shows the billionth in order? | *the billionth visitor to the website | billions of visitors | the first visitor to the website | a billion visitors all at once
exam: Which is smaller: a billionth of a metre or a millionth of a metre? | A millionth of a metre | *A billionth of a metre | They are the same size | You cannot tell from the words
